OL,3,GNEWSAGive our southern villages tourism
OL,4,Aboost, say families
OL,5,
OL,6,FResidents in the south of the Isle of
OL,7,FMan have called for a fresh boost for
OL,8,Ftourism ahead of the island's
OL,9,Fforthcoming election, as well as
OL,10,Fhighlighting pressures on local shops
OL,11,Fand concerns about young people.
OL,13,FThe island's southern-most
OL,14,Fconstituency, Rushen, takes in the
OL,15,Fvillages of Port Erin and Port St Mary
OL,16,Falong with its namesake parish.
OL,18,FTraditionally dominated by fishing and
OL,19,Ffarming, the seaside villages went on
OL,20,Fto benefit from the so-called "bucket
OL,21,Fand spade brigade" tourist boom - which
OL,22,Flater fell into decline.
OL,23,APub: 18-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
